course: dictionary
lesson: 11175
title: Winking words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A wink is very quick. You close and open one eye in a flash, and it often tells someone a joke, a secret or that you are friendly. «Later Grandad winks at you» means he is sharing something private, not that something is wrong with his eye.
explain: Use the words around wink to find its meaning. «Hold a finger at arm's length and wink one eye, then the other» is about the action. «I haven't had a wink of sleep» uses wink as a noun, so the words «sleep» and «these three weeks» tell you it means any sleep at all.
explain: Wink has other meanings too. «After lunch Badger takes forty winks» is an informal phrase meaning a short nap, not forty blinks. Ask yourself: does the sentence make sense with my meaning swapped in? If it does, you have found the right one.
explain: Remember your safety rule. If a stranger winks at you or asks you to keep a secret, tell a trusted adult straight away.
fact: Wink means to close and open one eye quickly, often to show a joke, a secret or friendliness.
fact: Wink can be a verb (winks, winked, winking) or a noun (a wink).
fact: Of a light, wink means to flash on and off.
fact: «Not sleep a wink» means not sleep at all.
fact: «Forty winks» means a short nap.
exercise: «Later Grandad winks at you.» What does the wink most likely show? | He has something stuck in his eye | He is going to sleep | He is angry with you | *He is sharing a joke or a friendly secret
exercise: «After lunch Badger takes forty winks.» What does forty winks mean? | Forty quick blinks | Forty pounds | *A short nap | A long journey
exercise: «Hold a finger at arm's length and wink one eye, then the other.» Find and copy the word that means to close and open one eye quickly. | *wink | finger | arm | wall
test: «I haven't had a wink of sleep these three weeks.» What does wink mean here? | A loud snore | *Not even a little sleep | A sleepy yawn | A quick blink
test: The lighthouse light began to wink across the dark sea. What does wink mean here? | To fall asleep | *To flash on and off | To shout across the water | To close one eye
exam: If a stranger winks at you and asks you to keep a secret, what should you do? | Keep the secret and say nothing | Go with them to find out more | Wink back at them | *Tell a trusted adult straight away
